  "examples": [{"id":"text-summary","title":"Text summary","category":"Content","apps":["An AI model"],"decider":"No one: the summary is written on its own","description":"When someone pastes a text into the page, the configured AI model writes a short factual summary of it. The page shows the summary with the model that wrote it and the tokens it used, and marks one the model cut short. A blank or too long text is refused before any paid request, and a refused or failed answer is shown with what went wrong instead of a summary. Without its optional model connection, the page remains available and summaries show how to connect an LLM."},{"id":"github-releases-newsletter","title":"GitHub releases newsletter","category":"Content","apps":["Slack","GitHub","OpenAI","Gmail"],"decider":"An administrator posting in Slack","description":"Visitors subscribe once with their email address on the page. When an administrator posts publish newsletter in the Slack channel, the process reads the last seven days of releases of two GitHub repositories, has OpenAI write one factual report, and sends it to every subscriber as their own Gmail message. A failed read or model answer sends nothing, and an uncertain send is never repeated."},{"id":"slack-thread-approval","title":"Slack thread approval","category":"Approvals","apps":["Slack"],"decider":"The members allowed to reply in the thread","description":"When someone posts a new message in the approval channel in Slack, a process starts for that thread and waits. The first reply in the thread from one of the members allowed to approve finishes it: the process posts “Processing complete.” in the thread. Later replies change nothing, and a message Slack delivers twice starts only one process."},{"id":"summary-approval","title":"Summary approval","category":"Approvals","apps":["An AI model"],"decider":"A person in Studio","description":"When someone pastes a text into the page, the configured AI model writes a short summary of it, and the summary waits for a person to approve it in Studio before it is saved. A truncated summary is saved without waiting, and a blocked, refused or failed answer is recorded with what went wrong instead of a summary. Without its optional model connection, the page remains available and summaries show how to connect an LLM."}],
